SettingsTest
├── getSettings
│   ├── given nothing has ever been stored
│   │   └── it returns the defaults
│   ├── given a partial record from an older version
│   │   ├── it fills in missing fields from the defaults
│   │   └── it keeps the stored values
│   ├── given a corrupted record
│   │   ├── given currencies is not an array
│   │   │   └── it restores the default list
│   │   ├── given the site lists are not arrays
│   │   │   └── it restores empty lists
│   │   └── given precision is missing
│   │       └── it restores the default precision
│   └── given the user deliberately enabled no currencies
│       └── it respects the empty list
├── watchSettings
│   ├── when the stored value changes
│   │   └── it reports the change filled in with defaults
│   └── when the caller unsubscribes
│       └── it stops reporting
├── setSettings
│   ├── it merges over what is already stored
│   └── it leaves untouched fields alone
└── migration from sync storage
    ├── given there is nothing in sync storage
    │   └── it does nothing
    ├── given sync storage holds settings
    │   ├── given local storage is empty
    │   │   ├── it copies them to local
    │   │   └── it removes the sync copy
    │   └── given local storage already holds settings
    │       ├── it keeps the local values
    │       └── it removes the sync copy
    ├── given sync storage is unavailable
    │   └── it falls through to local without failing
    └── given two callers migrate at once
        └── it migrates exactly once
